invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw one-pass open hashes each pass after it has decrypted
  it, where the loop hashes each pass one iteration before. An open into
  a second buffer cannot show the difference, because the ciphertext
  stays as it was; an open in place, which quic_packet.c's is, hashes the
  plaintext it just wrote over the ciphertext and refuses every genuine
  packet past 128 bytes. bin/ghash_equiv_test opens in place and below
  the ciphertext as well as into a second buffer, and requires the
  plaintext back.

--- old
            xor_pass_in_place(s.keystream, &in[at], &out[at]);
        }
        if (p < passes) {
            ghash_hash_pass(&s.ghash, &in[p * GCM_HW_PASS_BYTES]);
        }
--- new
            xor_pass_in_place(s.keystream, &in[at], &out[at]);
            ghash_hash_pass(&s.ghash, &in[at]);
        }
